  "notes": "Indecency: nothing drawn, no people; a scroll for the testimony, a door for «سبيلا», a leaf for reform, light and an hourglass for repentance «من قريب», geometric near Allah's names. 15-16 carry both tafsirs' point that this was the ruling of early Islam (glosses kept to definitions; the confinement line has no gloss so no command is shown without its condition). STAGING v4: 15-16 stay ambient with no people on screen: the ruling on indecency (private matter). 17: one man in a prayer hall; the evil deed is never acted; he bows in regret on 17:10 (they repent), raises his hands on 17:12 (soon), then prays (Al-Muyassar: يرجعون إلى ربهم بالإنابة والطاعة). Light plate on the repentance, hourglass on 17:12 ended before the Name, geometric for the closing names."
 },
